 number of messages linking to each bin (after removing cis-linkages)."],["Supplementary Table 2 p1","We empirically computed a significance threshold of 12 messages per bin"],["Supplementary Table 2 p1","Twenty-two bins fit this criterion."],["Supplementary Table 2 p1","Group 2 contains linkages from four bins, Group 11 from three bins, and Groups 3, 7, 8, and 12 from two bins each."],["Supplementary Table 2 p1","Group 2 contains the cluster of 12 genes shown in Figure 1 of the main text, whose regulator we confirmed to be Amn1."],["Supplementary Table 2 p3","Group 7 contains the cluster of 7 pheromone response genes shown in Figure 1 of the main text, whose regulator we confirmed to be GPA1."],["Supplementary Table 2 p2","Multiple additional regulators may control subsets of the 197 Group 2 genes"],["Supplementary Table 2 p2","Group 4 contains 100 messages linking to a region near the gene LEU2 (an auxotrophic marker deleted in the RM strain)."],["Supplementary Table 2 p2","The 36 messages of Group 5 map to the MAT locus."],["Supplementary Table 2 p2","Group 6 contains 19 messages linking to the URA3 locus (another auxotrophic marker deleted in the RM strain)."],["Supplementary Table 2 p3","We showed previously that our BY strain carries a Ty insertion in HAP1"],["Supplementary Table 2 p3","The messages in Group 9 link to a region on chromosome XII containing SIR3."],["Supplementary Table 2 p3","A good candidate in the linkage region is CAT5"],["Supplementary Table 2 p2","A good candidate is the RNA helicase MAK5"],["Supplementary Table 2 p4","Group 11 contains 380 messages"]]}}